nk 22 the required kernel-intersection dimension drops below the minimal orbit dimension allowable by the symmetry group—and even lists a countercondition testing whether an equivalent obstruction fails at <2,2,2>. Yet simulation_refs is empty []. The problem explicitly requires that discriminating experiments be filed as sandboxed Python simulations and states that prose with empty simulation_refs is an unverified claim. The kernel-dimension / orbit-dimension inequality is exactly the kind of statement that can be evaluated by integer arithmetic on a smaller decidable format, making the absence of any simulation a direct failure of the problem's verification requirement.","counterexample":null,"target_alias":"SRC_003"}]}